  <title>Vendor history</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Vendor</gui><gui>Vendor history</gui></guiseq> lists
  purchase orders and their lines.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Vendor</gui>, or check <gui>All vendors</gui>.
    <gui>Total</gui> adds up the orders listed.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select an order to see its lines below, or check <gui>All
    products</gui> for the lines of every order.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type into the search boxes to narrow the lines down by product,
    ext name, remark or order number.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <list>
    <item><p>Double click an order to open it as it was printed.</p></item>
    <item><p>Right click an order for its <link xref="purchase_order_hub">PO
    hub</link>, or <gui>View attachment</gui> to see the vendor's invoice.
    If none is attached yet, <gui>View attachment</gui> lets you attach one;
    see <link xref="pdf_attachment"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Right click a line for its <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Drag a line onto an open <link xref="purchase_order"/> to order
    the same product again.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Refresh vendors</gui> and <gui>Refresh POs</gui> load the
    lists again.</p></item>
  </list>

  <section id="edit">
  <title>Edit mode</title>
  <p>Check <gui>Edit mode</gui> in the window menu to rename orders and change
  their descriptions in the list, and to replace an order's attachment with
  <gui>Edit attachment</gui>. It asks for the administrator password; see
  <link xref="main_window#admin"/>. <gui>Save window layout</gui> remembers
  the window's size and column widths on this computer.</p>
  </section>

</page>
